# ES8311 codec driver tests

Exercises the ES8311 driver against a recording MCU platform that answers as
the codec and an I2S transmitter do: identification, the reset and power-up
transcript, the clock program for both slot widths, configure's refusals and
reconfiguration, the Out contract -- a pending run kept through zero and
partial acceptance and through an error, the Stream read only when nothing is
pending, each sample in both slots, silence reported as underrun, position,
pending, stop, and restart -- and sleep. The transmitter consumes a frame only
when a case ticks it. No hardware is involved.
